---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Asterium Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Asterium grimoire app for magic and witchcraft."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Asterium Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: July 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Asterium is a digital grimoire application designed for magic and witchcraft, 
          allowing users to explore, create, and organize their personal spiritual practices.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information Asterium collects, how it interact 
          with our shared backend database, and how you retain complete ownership and control 
          over your spiritual data.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sign in with Apple</h2>
        <p>
          Asterium requires user authentication via Apple's "Sign in with Apple" framework 
          to securely identify your account across your iOS and iPadOS devices.
        </p>

        <p>
          This authentication process is securely insulated by Apple, meaning your raw personal 
          credentials or password information are never shared with or known to our systems.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Stored Data & Cloud Database</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike some of our other database-free applications, Asterium connects securely 
          to your account's dedicated repository within our shared TypeScript backend and MongoDB 
          Atlas cluster.
        </p>

        <p>
          To ensure you can securely access your custom creations across devices, Asterium stores 
          your custom, AI-generated correspondences and personal spells inside this database. 
          No other telemetry or personal background data is held.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>AI Generation Features</h2>
        <p>
          Asterium provides optional AI-driven features to help brainstorm and generate custom 
          spells or magical correspondences. 
        </p>

        <p>
          The prompts you submit to these tools are processed securely via approved AI service 
          providers solely to return your requested spiritual output, and are never used to 
          train persistent language models or profile your behavior.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Asterium firmly maintains a zero-advertising policy. We do not sell your personal data, 
          and your magical records, spell titles, and correspondences are completely hidden from 
          third-party advertisers, brokers, or data analytics trackers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Total Control & Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          We believe your spiritual path should remain entirely under your authority. Asterium 
          includes a clear, permanent deletion mechanism directly within the application.
        </p>

        <p>
          By navigating to your profile page, you can tap the data removal button to instantly and 
          permanently wipe all of your stored spells, AI-generated correspondences, and account 
          records from both the local device and our MongoDB Atlas database servers entirely.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new grimoire modules, 
          security protocols, or adjustments to our backend infrastructure.
        </p>

        <p>
          Any revised terms will be published straight to this web page with an updated 
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or wish to inquire about the security 
          of your digital grimoire data, you can reach out directly via our portal:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(24px);
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--overlay-gradient-accent);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
